 call #registerFragmentHeaders instead."],["6f6f8dbf_80197d11",46,-2,1,"Use the new instanceof syntax for better readability."],["722c52f0_62fa6b18",48,-2,1,"I think this will face a problem for a fragment like AdaptiveToolbarSettingsFragment that may appear at one of the 2 different locations in the tree depending on a feature flag i.e. its parent can be…"],["93ad8fc5_f0cea98c",48,-2,1,"IIUC we're looping through all index data providers per each index data provider, which results in O(N^2) complexity, not the most efficient approach. Should we consider a more performant one?"],["ba20333c_9d961450",48,-2,1,"New instanceof syntax will save you from having to cast |childProvider|"],["e0ae7216_ddef0cf0",48,-2,1,"Feels like we're putting another substantial amount of code back into BaseSearchIndexProvider. Can this be pulled out, like we did with initPreferenceXml?"],["01fa1729_7ce7f24a",44,-1,1,"nit: Define this method below the caller."],["393775f9_d9e0c3f1",47,-1,1,"Can this ever happen? I'd prefer having an assert instead."],["416a6c2a_53e7ee08",49,-1,0,"Same question - why is this null check needed?"],["5f60a18a_ea8cd561",49,-1,0,"When can this header be null?"],["63c9cabd_cf7a0fc7",47,-1,1,"Are there any preferences without a key? I wonder if we can do without the check."],["63fe0cb5_346fe693",44,-1,0,"Can initPreferenceXml and updateDynamicPreferences be in a single loop?"],["89794962_790e9669",44,-1,1,"This comment doesn't seem useful. May be removed"],["8daa2f76_34218e16",49,-1,0,"ditto"],["9ad2e595_692be037",50,-1,1,"* Move this above |initPreferenceXml| as this is invoked first. * This method should always be implemented, right? Remove |default| if so."],["9f6dbf92_ccd333fc",47,-1,1,"This comment and the one below sound redundant."],["c9d55f4c_9a98a5cd",46,-1,1,"May be removed"],["d9f84ae2_0bb53681",49,-1,1,"This method looks important, and deserves a javadoc"],["da4a3637_06bf22df",48,-1,1,"Now that I see it again, the check here doesn't look necessary - the